 86	| `local-emulator` | `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT`, `FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST` | Firestore emulator | Shared local development and integration tests |
 87	| `gcp` | Application Default Credentials; optional explicit `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` | Managed Firestore | Deployed environments |
 88	
 89	Outside Cloud Run, an unset mode defaults to `memory` for compatibility with
 90	the current Compose demo. Cloud Run selects `gcp` automatically, rejects an
 91	explicit `memory` or `local-emulator` mode, and detects the project ID through
 92	Application Default Credentials or the metadata server when
 93	`GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` is not set. A deployed service therefore cannot silently
 94	start with ephemeral state or emulator credentials.
 95	
 96	Managed emulator and GCP servers return redacted public lost-pet records.
 97	Contact, match/reunion transition, and push-subscription endpoints remain
 98	disabled with `403 Forbidden` outside explicit `memory` demo mode until
 99	issue #110 adds authentication and ownership enforcement.
100	
101	For example, after starting a Firestore emulator on port 8085:
102	
103	```bash
104	export PETSPOTR_RUNTIME_MODE=local-emulator
105	export GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=petspotr-local
106	export FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8085
107	export PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8086
