237	
238	Durable events store only the finalized object name. The matcher reads that
239	private object with its service identity and base64-encodes the bytes for
240	Ollama; no public or expiring URL is placed in an event. Private read URLs are
241	V4-signed and capped at 15 minutes. Existing URL events remain readable during
242	the schema migration, but managed found-pet report creation rejects them.
243	
244	The bucket enforces public access prevention and uniform access. Set
245	`image_cors_allowed_origins` to exact deployed web origins; the default empty
246	list permits no browser origin. Unfinalized `uploads/` objects are deleted
247	after one day. The found-pet process also reconciles at most 100 finalized
248	objects per pass with a cursor. After a 24-hour grace period—well beyond the
249	15-minute capability and two-minute report deadlines—it deletes an object only
250	when two durable-state checks find no report referencing the exact name and the
251	object generation is unchanged. This recovers the crash window between GCS
252	finalization and the Firestore report transaction without deleting active,
253	referenced, or replaced objects. The capability authenticates the generated
254	report upload; tying that capability to a signed-in user remains tracked by
255	issue #110. Routing the browser through the canonical service remains tracked
256	by issue #113.
